== DESIGN (one mechanism changed, everything else stands) ==
- godot/scripts/lane_bands.gd (86 lines): paint_lane_bands(m) per ground lane mounts
  a band Node3D named LaneBand_<id> carrying ONE MeshInstance3D per waypoint segment:
  mesh = unit PlaneMesh (PrimitiveMesh — engine-managed geometry; default size 1x1,
  the node scale carries dimensions), position = segment midpoint at y BAND_Y,
  rotation.y = atan2(-d.z, d.x) (local +X walks the segment, +Z the lateral normal —
  same orientation as G2's hand-built normal n=(-d.z,0,d.x)), scale = (segment
  length, 1, BAND_WIDTH); material = the SAME pinned shape (unshaded +
  TRANSPARENCY_ALPHA + BAND_COLOR), one instance per band, applied via
  material_override (the arena-ground rasterize-proven path). Degenerate segment
  (<0.001 u) returns null instead of a zero-scale/NaN-rotation node. ZERO writes on
  m; m.map_def never read.
- Kit godot/sim/g2_lane_band_probe.gd (232 lines, boot idiom unchanged): rows now
  LB-BANDS n=3 ground=3 / LB-BAND <lid> segs=N mat=1 (band at origin + one
  MeshInstance3D child per wp segment + pinned material per segment) / LB-CLASS <lid>
  mesh=PlaneMesh prim=1 segs=N — THE WEB-PROOF PROXY rows (every segment mesh IS a
  PlaneMesh AND a PrimitiveMesh; class name printed from get_class()) / LB-WPS
  (endpoint pins: unit-plane ±X ends via to_global of each NODE land on the
  segment's two wps within EPS 0.05 — wp-follow through the band NODE/segment
  midpoints) / LB-NEG air=2 banded=0. Completion-flag idiom + planted-red
  (suppress one ground band -> BANDS row RED) carried over from G2 unchanged.
- tests/test_lane_bands.py (5 legs, was 4; net +1): engine probe rows incl. the
  LB-CLASS proxy rows (segs per lane DERIVED from gatefall.json, not double-pinned);
  mount source-truth (unchanged — mission_world still one call, no geometry);
  builder source-truth updated (one Node3D band site, ONE MeshInstance3D segment
  site, zero-writes regex, literal "ground" filter) + NEW test_builder_rides_
  primitive_mesh_geometry_source_truth: PlaneMesh.new() built once, and NO retired-
  mechanism token (ArrayMesh/add_surface_from_arrays/ARRAY_VERTEX/ARRAY_INDEX/
  PackedVector3Array/PackedInt32Array) survives in CODE — the header comment naming
  the retired mechanism is stripped before the scan (comments are stripped because
  the header must be allowed to explain WHY the file reads the way it does; the
  runtime LB-CLASS rows police real geometry). Data leg unchanged.
- WEB-PROOF LEG declaration (per brief): served-browser pixel re-check: ORCHESTRATOR
  (expected >20k band-tinted px on build-phase frame). The machine-checkable proxy
  legs are the probe's LB-CLASS rows + the test's primitive-geometry source leg; if
  the orchestrator's served-browser re-shoot does not cross the bar the card comes
